 {:db/id "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c637c93-1ee3-58ef-993c-3c6e5c1fc84b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8"] :answer-field/correct "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-338982" :question/id #uuid "76fbcb9f-680c-51b9-b052-efdce55007dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-338982" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+3y=0,\\,y(1)={y}^{′}(3)=0,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(3) & {y}_{2}^{′}(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem has a unique solution if and only if {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$   \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have Robin boundary conditions given by\n\n$$\ny(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, setting ${\\alpha }_{1}=1,$ ${\\beta }_{1}=0,$ ${\\alpha }_{2}=0,$ ${\\beta }_{2}=1,$ and $a=1,$ $b=3,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(3) & {y}_{2}^{′}(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-4m+3 & =0 \\\\ (m-1)(m-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have ${m}_{1}=1$ and ${m}_{2}=3,$ and so the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\text{and}\\,{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1} & {e}^{3(1)} \\\\ {e}^{3} & 3{e}^{3(3)}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}e & {e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & 3{e}^{9}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =e(3{e}^{9})-{e}^{3}({e}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{10}-{e}^{6} \\\\  & ={e}^{6}(3{e}^{4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has the unique solution }y≡0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338982/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485" "q-338982/ma-source-field/bbf154adee8f0ae4bad077f4defb7855896bbb5b4a9db96754635faa307e4a70" "q-338982/ma-source-field/43a35218b1cf23450e4e061cffa2a4a6e8e5b1bbad2021d4dc7405327bcce8f2" "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
