 {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4" :answer-field/id #uuid "40c6d291-cf90-51ae-b2e3-e5400146213f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/3106d29ec84ff4a540fd8dad587c31084ffb5bcb597f43d1abcf43548fc86090" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/61b414f03fb19f29a438aafd2c26809ce879d88ba614d981b6366b238a05ca82" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/ecdf59a6922e0a715d091f39d1edb555e71827b1cef672bec6f966d7329a486d" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/ccfdfe1553bd07a74184fa884521de80a6a997a2cb3a9bc67957d68dfb3f0e82"] :answer-field/correct "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-339145" :question/id #uuid "b18cb65d-b781-5075-91bf-6c656ac3ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339145" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y=x,\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/6)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =\\int 6{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}+C \\\\ y & =6+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =6+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/12} \\\\ 5 & =6+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
