 {:db/id "q-339176/ma-source-field/54c8085c508b42ef2dd009bc2421d72af83d38aafdba0ecde85a42208feb1051" :answer-field/id #uuid "e53b80d8-ad34-5531-b34b-01b41813b9b4" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-339176/ma-source-field/54c8085c508b42ef2dd009bc2421d72af83d38aafdba0ecde85a42208feb1051/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" "q-339176/ma-source-field/54c8085c508b42ef2dd009bc2421d72af83d38aafdba0ecde85a42208feb1051/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" "q-339176/ma-source-field/54c8085c508b42ef2dd009bc2421d72af83d38aafdba0ecde85a42208feb1051/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8"] :answer-field/correct "q-339176/ma-source-field/54c8085c508b42ef2dd009bc2421d72af83d38aafdba0ecde85a42208feb1051/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-339176" :question/id #uuid "355bfeb1-d0b8-53cd-b763-3f92856140f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-339176" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4y=0,\\,2y(0)-{y}^{′}(0)=2y(1)-{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}(0)-{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & 2{y}_{2}(0)-{y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ 2{y}_{1}(1)-{y}_{1}^{′}(1) & 2{y}_{2}(1)-{y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem has a unique solution if and only if {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i}$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have mixed (Robin) boundary conditions. So, setting ${\\alpha }_{i}=2,$ ${\\beta }_{i}=-1,$ $a=0,$ and $b=1,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}(0)-{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & 2{y}_{2}(0)-{y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ 2{y}_{1}(1)-{y}_{1}^{′}(1) & 2{y}_{2}(1)-{y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ (m-2)(m+2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=2$ and $m=-2,$ and so the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}\\text{ and }{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x},\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=-2{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4{e}^{-2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =0(4{e}^{-2})-0(4) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=0$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has infinitely many solutions }.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339176/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485" "q-339176/ma-source-field/3fe59a9f7619d4e72a50bb79e1e94cf2d6aafddcb987c329536882025c799dfa" "q-339176/ma-source-field/12062564ad198d757c1667add49cbde2aed9b3e3670fa4f94879e557c55fb10f" "q-339176/ma-source-field/54c8085c508b42ef2dd009bc2421d72af83d38aafdba0ecde85a42208feb1051"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
