 {:db/id "q-340669" :question/id #uuid "3d6ca311-b229-51f5-b6ee-b805697465fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-340669" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992" "q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
