 {:db/id "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a55cae0b-d0e7-5c92-b5d3-5cd9673f9f43" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1/ccd37af225235e99e0c0beacf5c114a7061b025eb104267b602d298657c10927" "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1/619b81cb1e10d64e3031268fbdcd0788831828a8749a0c18fe0c45867dd31ec5" "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5" "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1/9aa9dfbc88f5063553a847c368b29cb8dda581610b843fa8c8f6be915eb97944" "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1/6a46260098fce3dc291803fdba96a1a712933fdeee4d8c5b5bb67cc07cfd19c0"] :answer-field/correct "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1/ccd37af225235e99e0c0beacf5c114a7061b025eb104267b602d298657c10927" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-341448" :question/id #uuid "d8e97793-b7f7-5bb2-8257-c5344e5ddb06" :question/math-academy-id "q-341448" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}2,\\, & t\\le 3 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\, & t>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}2,\\, & t\\le 3 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\, & t>3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{t-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 1.$\n\nFor $s>1,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{3}+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{{e}^{(1-s)t}}{1-s})|}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{1-s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{(1-s)a}-{e}^{3(1-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{1-s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{3(1-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341448/ma-source-field/be2b567a955e9b13a1dd37ef10726ee88f68b964ce253e6ad5059251b0efc807" "q-341448/ma-source-field/81512949606164691d893d745fd7a8a974b05f098d82b489afac43b1382e4de1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
